            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run: what did atithi mean, and what did raita mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ನಿಜ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಿಜ (nija) — \"true\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit nija began as 'one's own, innate, born in' — what belongs to a thing by nature rather than by accident."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kannada and Telugu both took that and turned it toward truth, and you can watch the turn happen inside the word: what is true of a thing is what the thing is in itself, as against what is merely said about it. Said alone, ನಿಜ (nija) does the work of a whole sentence — 'true', 'that's right'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five replies that do more than agree or refuse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "nija",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *nija*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "nija, then haudu, and hear how much more the first one claims",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *nija*, then *haudu*, and hear how much more the first one claims]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does ನಿಜ (nija) mean? (\"true\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
