          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಸಾಕು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಾಕು (sāku) — \"enough\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಾಕು (sāku) is a complete sentence with one word in it. Held up over a plate while someone is ladling rice, it means 'that's enough' and stops the ladle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No Sanskrit anywhere in it — ಸಾಕು (sāku) is Kannada's own, resting on an inherited verb for sufficing. It covers a whole English shelf on its own: enough, plenty, stop, that will do. Kannada is content to let the situation and the tone sort out which."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: true, and enough."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
