        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹಾಗೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಾಗೆ (hāge) — \"that way, just so\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಾಗೆ (hāge) means 'that way, like that', and offered on its own it agrees: 'just so'. ಹಾಗೇ ಆಗಲಿ — let it be that way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now set it beside ಹೇಗೆ, the question word for 'how' that this book gave you early on. They differ in one vowel. Supply the third and the shape is complete:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೀಗೆ — this way. ಹಾಗೆ (hāge) — that way. ಹೇಗೆ — which way?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the same three-way grid as ಇದು, ಅದು and ಎಲ್ಲಿ: ಇ- for what is near, ಅ- for what is away, ಎ- for what is being asked about. Kannada builds a great many of its small words on those three vowels, and once you can hear them you stop learning such words one at a time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five replies: true, enough, certainly, perhaps, just so."
            }
          ]
        },
